y and and the health care  requirement  rather that only numbers concerning the  detection so like  seven days incidence or rt number  so you say that's what you're currently  focusing on does the number  that's most important change over time  this this change of course um  we have been tracking them essentially  since the beginning of the pandemic it  became quite clear that the  disease require or might have a severe  course  and end up in debts or require  hospitalization and  health care and this is  of course an indicator which  which is not stable depends very much on  the on the  on the healthcare capacity of the  country but  i believe is less affected uh from  tracking capacities or testing activity  in the country so  we have all these numbers the r number  the seven day incidences and stuff  do the general public need to be across  these numbers i can understand  why governments and decision makers  might need to be but what about  can't we just stay at home and do as  we're told without getting caught up in  the figures  well i guess it's probably the first  time  um at least since i'm aware of that and  as far the first time that people became  so informed about  the the meaning of reproduction number  or even  seven days incident for any disease um  these numbers are reported for a number  of diseases but usually are kept in in  in control systems in healthcare  facilities so  people were working with that so now it  they went into the community and i guess  it was because  of making people aware making people um  aware of the severity of the pandemic of  of the  the way weight spreads um but of course  the the number of the numbers uh that we  get or the more numbers that we get  this can make people more confused they  might not know what they you're looking  at it's  there are some indicators like the  reproduction number  or which which is not like temperature  measurement  it depends on on on the cases that are  reported  and these are in case of